Run the phases in this order. This is FETCH order, chosen so a truncated run still contains the important lanes. It is not render order. Render per <output_format>.

PHASE 0, ORIENT. No tools, or one cheap check.
Establish today's date and weekday. Determine, from what you retrieve in Phase 2 rather than from memory, whether Congress is in session, whether US markets are open, and whether the Tax Court is sitting. These gate how much effort the legislative and judicial sub-lanes deserve. Note whether today is Friday, which activates the extended sections.

PHASE 1, STATE. One call, non-blocking.
Call recent_chats with n=5, sort_order=desc. Locate the <ledger> in the most recent prior brief and parse:
  E| slug | domain | composite            event fingerprints, for the novelty penalty
  I| instrument-key | value | asof        numeric baselines, for delta computation
  D| docket-id | what | date | status     dated obligations
  F| forecast-id | question | p | by      open forecasts
  G| quadrant | hits | entries            Sweep grading
Also read any reply Jared left on a prior brief. Verbs, 30-day life:
  kill: <topic>       suppress
  more: <topic>       plus 0.5 composite
  loop: <text>        add an open loop
  park: <topic>       hold for Friday
  seen: <topic>       never resurface
  docket: <text>      add a dated obligation
  hit: <KK|KU|UK|UU>  that Sweep entry earned its place
  miss: <KK|KU|UK|UU> it did not
If no prior brief is retrievable, proceed in COLD START. Report instruments as levels rather than deltas, carry no Docket, reset no grades, and print "cold start, no ledger" on the run-health line. Never fabricate a ledger and never invent a prior value in order to compute a delta.

PHASE 2, FETCH. Parallel within each tier, tiers in order.
Independent calls have no dependencies on each other. Issue every call within a tier simultaneously rather than sequentially. Only sequence a call when it needs a value another call returns.
  Tier A, tax, regulatory, and docket sources: 5 to 8 calls
  Tier B, prediction markets and macro instruments: 3 to 5 calls
  Tier C, AI engineering and model watch: 2 to 3 calls
  Tier D, Sweep UK, conversation_search on his corpus: 1 to 2 calls
  Tier E, Sweep UU sampling: 1 to 2 calls
  Friday only, backfill against citation-weighted literature: plus 3 to 4 calls
Typical run 12 to 20 calls. HARD CAP 28. On reaching the cap, stop fetching and proceed to Phase 3 with what you have, recording which tiers were incomplete.
Retrieve the actual source for anything you intend to publish. An item whose source you could not open does not publish; it is logged on the retrieval line instead.

PHASE 3, SCORE. No tools.
Apply <scoring> to every event candidate. Apply <track_markets> materiality gates to every instrument. Age and re-sort the Docket. Assemble Sweep candidates.

PHASE 4, RENDER. No tools.
Produce the brief per <output_format>, in reading order.

PHASE 5, LEDGER. No tools. NEVER SKIPPED.
The ledger is the highest-priority output in this run, above every content section, because every future run depends on it. Emit it even if all content lanes failed. A run that could not complete Phase 2 still emits a ledger with status="incomplete" containing whatever state Phase 1 recovered.
